  THE RAMP EXEMPTION DOES NOT CLEAR THE dF1 BAR AT THIS n.
  Read the `aligned` and `thr drift` columns before calling it a
  null -- at n = 18 the dF1 bar is ~17 Hz and the exponent says what
  this mechanism could possibly have delivered into it.

  What r1 did: aligned x0.957, gain 2.43 -> 2.24, larynx 7.79 Hz
  against the shipped 5.58, threshold push +1.441 against +1.415.
  Against the two earlier reliefs -- v57 pooling HALVED the learned
  bias and pushed the threshold 3x harder; `ipoff` collapsed learning
  outright at -7.42 SE (both on file, not this run).

  AND `aligned` does NOT clear v58's x1.21 at 2 SE, so this is not
  an established win over the earlier reliefs. Whether it is the
  same closure again or merely underpowered is what the SE on the
  ratio says -- read it, do not read the point estimate.

  And ^0.61 turns this run's aligned into -2.6 Hz, a bar needing 0
  seeds against the 18 it ran. The ceiling is one exponent and not a
  tally of dead ends: dF1 x1.68 wants aligned x2.34, and every knob
  this project has found moves it x1.1-x1.2. If the ramp exemption is
  in that band too, then the regulator's COORDINATE SYSTEM was not the
  thing holding the ceiling down, and what is left is the readout
  itself -- a rate-weighted centroid, by design.
